abstract: >-
  Euclid's roofs on a cube make the regular dodecahedron; folding the roof
  vertices back through the cube faces makes the regular icosahedron, edges
  φ² : φ : 1, each roof vertex landing on a neighbouring cell's icosahedron.
  On a simple cubic lattice: 13 nodes per cell, Pm-3, with every cell's 31
  icosahedral axes aligned. Great stellated dodecahedra on the even cells and
  icosahedra on the odd cells share only corners (the Euclid–Kepler–Pacioli network).
  Every claim is checked by krp-core's scripts/verify-roof-fold.mjs (github.com/DICTOR-Master/krp-core). See DISCOVERIES.md #8.
